---
title: Create your instructor account
description: Sign in with Authentik to open your teacher space. GitHub is only needed later, when you submit the course.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

To teach at Librería de Satoshi you need an instructor account. It's separate from your campus account: the campus one is for *taking* courses, this one for *proposing* them.

## Signing in

{% steps %}

1. Open [ismos.xyz/become-a-teacher](https://ismos.xyz/become-a-teacher/). You can also get there from [/entrar](/en/acceso/entrar/) by choosing **I'm a teacher**.

2. Press **Continue with Authentik**.

3. We redirect you to Authentik to authorise your instructor account. If you don't have one, you create it right there.

4. You come back to your instructor space, signed in.

{% /steps %}

{% aside type="caution" title="If sign-in fails" %}
If you see *"We couldn't complete sign-in with Authentik"*, try again. It's usually an authorisation that was left half-done, not a problem with your account.
{% /aside %}

## What you see once you're in

Your instructor space picks up where you left off and has four blocks:

- **Identity** — your Authentik account. Completed as soon as you sign in.
- **Instructor profile** — who you are and your experience. [Filled in here](/en/profesores/perfil/).
- **GitHub attribution** — the identity your course will be signed with. [Connected here](/en/profesores/github/), and if you don't have an account yet, [created here](/en/profesores/cuenta-github/).
- **Your course** — the [proposal form](/en/profesores/crear-curso/).

At the top you also have **Go to Moodle** and **Sign out**.

## GitHub isn't needed yet

You can start building your course before connecting GitHub. It's only required to **submit** the proposal, because the course lives and gets reviewed on GitHub.

{% aside title="Pseudonym" %}
If you'd rather not use your real name, create a new GitHub account without it. That's a decision to make before connecting the account, not after: we have a [guide to creating the account](/en/profesores/cuenta-github/) covering what you'll need to decide along the way.
{% /aside %}

## Everything saves itself

Autosave is on in both the profile and the course form. You can close the tab halfway through and carry on another day from the same point.
